{#- Structured host-list status cell: a status dot, a short state word and a live
    relative time -- never a fully-resolved sentence. Quarantine wins and is LOUD.
    The dot, the wording and its emphasis are FACTS on HostState, so no state can render
    green (or quiet) by falling through a branch this template forgot. The words and the time
    are ONE run of text beside the dot: as two flex items they wrapped as two columns
    ("Docker 29.7.1, seen" beside "2 hours ago") in a narrow name column. -#}
{% declare value: HostStatusCell %}
{% if value != null %}
<span class="hh-host-state" data-host-state={% value.stateToken %}>
    <pl-status-dot status={% value.dot %}></pl-status-dot>
    <span class="hh-host-state-text">{% if value.loud %}<strong class="hh-host-state-quarantined">{{ value.stateText }}</strong>{% else %}{{ value.stateText }}{% /if %}{% if value.lastSeenIso != null %} <pl-relative-time datetime={% value.lastSeenIso %} title={% value.lastSeenIso %}></pl-relative-time>{% /if %}</span>
</span>
{% /if %}
